<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ankara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1402</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> was fought in 1402 in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> and the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>. Timur won a crushing victory and captured Bayezid, who died in captivity. The battle displayed Timurid military supremacy and plunged the Ottoman state into a period of civil war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ankara.jpg" alt="Battle of Ankara" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1436 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timur_reviews_his_troops_in_the_plain_of_Sivas_in_the_battle_of_Ankara_in_mid-summer_1402._Zafarnama_of_1436,_facing_folios_356r_(left),_355v_(right).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
